n/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}(u+v)=\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{cos}v-\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{sin}v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot 0-\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234046 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "11214dee-7d32-5b34-bc7e-86bbedbaab36" :question/math-academy-id "q-43384" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}(u-v)=\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{cos}v+\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{sin}v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for cosine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\\left(x-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}x-\\operatorname{cos}x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1914e519-4beb-5bb8-9a38-50ed69e1d866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333216} {:answer/id #uuid "22a3763d-dc3d-5935-ae8